1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,478
One worn part can stop a favorite routine.

2
00:00:03,598 --> 00:00:09,684
Useful electronics sit in drawers because
no one knows what to do with them.

3
00:00:09,804 --> 00:00:12,847
Orphan Parts Lens starts with two
questions.

4
00:00:12,967 --> 00:00:16,880
What do you have, and what do you want?

5
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:21,937
This older Hamilton Beach drink mixer
makes frappé coffee.

6
00:00:22,057 --> 00:00:24,251
Its agitator is worn.

7
00:00:24,371 --> 00:00:32,600
The rod has no model number, so the app
asks which device it came from.

8
00:00:32,720 --> 00:00:36,560
The label under the base answers that.

9
00:00:36,680 --> 00:00:42,166
Search the web looks first for the maker's
own part.

10
00:00:42,286 --> 00:00:49,417
It keeps only pages the search returned,
each a listing with its link.

11
00:00:49,537 --> 00:00:55,571
Check fit turns every unknown into a
question for the seller.

12
00:00:55,691 --> 00:01:01,177
Decide weighs fixing, reusing or selling
against the owner's skills.

13
00:01:01,297 --> 00:01:07,880
It recommends keeping it and fixing it,
and the owner chooses that.

14
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:11,389
The same approach works for unused
electronics.

15
00:01:11,509 --> 00:01:17,318
Laptops, monitors and parts go into the
inventory, beside a skills profile.

16
00:01:17,438 --> 00:01:23,732
The preferences say what the build is for
and what it can cost.

17
00:01:23,852 --> 00:01:28,693
Muse Spark proposes projects from what is
in the inventory.

18
00:01:28,813 --> 00:01:32,686
The rules keep only what the inventory
backs.

19
00:01:32,806 --> 00:01:37,163
The arcade that was asked for isn't among
them.

20
00:01:37,283 --> 00:01:44,060
So the home automation server is selected,
and its laptop is committed to it.

21
00:01:44,180 --> 00:01:49,505
Draw it shows how it could look, marked as
a drawing.

22
00:01:49,625 --> 00:01:54,951
What is missing becomes a Marketplace
search that the owner runs.

23
00:01:55,071 --> 00:02:00,880
The build pack collects the items, the
steps, and the safety notes.

24
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:04,004
The graphics card is for sale.

25
00:02:04,124 --> 00:02:08,629
Price guidance keeps each figure apart,
with its sources.

26
00:02:08,749 --> 00:02:13,755
Muse Voice Transcribe turns a voice note
into its condition.

27
00:02:13,875 --> 00:02:17,880
The draft fills Marketplace's fields,
ready to paste.

28
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:22,811
On the phone, photos go into the same
inventory.

29
00:02:22,931 --> 00:02:29,880
The models are Muse Spark, SAM 3.1, Muse
Voice Transcribe and Muse Image.

30
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:36,044
Anyone can try it on the owner's own
photos.

31
00:02:36,164 --> 00:02:42,880
SAM 3.1 finds the label, then Muse Spark
reads it.

32
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:45,556
Orphan Parts Lens.

33
00:02:45,676 --> 00:02:47,380
Find replacements.

34
00:02:47,500 --> 00:02:49,204
Discover reuse.

35
00:02:49,324 --> 00:02:51,880
Build something useful.

